  "id": "immigration",
  "name": "Religious Immigration",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "note",
      "type": "Comment",
      "x": 20,
      "y": -130,
      "params": {
        "text": "Religious immigration (spec/systems/immigration.md, func_0363A2/035D9A/034C24). Per-turn crosses increment = base 2 + Sum(player colony populations = church/cathedral cross output); modeled here as 2 + colony0.population. A colonist arrives when the accumulator (+0x2E) crosses the needed threshold (+0x30 = baseNeed * (8-diff)/8, England x2/3). Arriving class is the byte-verified difficulty-weighted refill: roll(1,15) split by a difficulty cut into low-tier (criminals/servants/farmers) vs high-tier (Trained Mercenaries, or Educated Elite with William Brewster, FF 20). FLAGGED undecoded: baseNeed (func_035D9A table sum) and the split cut constant K in (diff+K)/2 -- here baseNeed=30, K=18 as placeholders."
      }
    },
